 "result": "All in `src/tessel/views.py`, using `VerbView` (a subclass of `View`):\n\n1. **Collecting methods:** `VerbView.__init_subclass__` (L165) runs when the class is defined. It scans for `get`, `post` and the other names in `http_method_funcs`, plus any methods inherited from base classes, and sets `cls.methods` (e.g. `{\"GET\", \"POST\"}`), unless the class already defines `methods` itself.\n2. **Making the view function:** `View.to_view_func(name)` (L86) is a classmethod that returns a plain function `view(**kwargs)`. It instantiates the class (once per request by default, or once up front if `init_every_request = False`) and calls `self.run_view` through `active_app.ensure_sync`. Any `decorators` are applied to it. It then copies `view_class`, `__name__`, `methods` and `provide_automatic_options` onto the function.\n3. **Registering:** `app.attach_route_rule(\"/x\", view_func=MyView.to_view_func(\"x\"))` (`src/tessel/sansio/app.py:606`) reads `view_func.methods` to decide which HTTP methods the rule accepts.\n4. **Dispatching:** `VerbView.run_view` (L182) looks up `getattr(self, request.method.lower())` and calls it with the URL kwargs. A `HEAD` request falls back to `get` when there is no `head` handler. If no handler is found, it fails an assertion.",
